  "review_state": "reviewed",
  "contract": "Datetime search attribute values and the per-run attribute limits (published Server 2.11.7 SearchAttributeValueValidator with Workflow 2.15.7 WorkflowSearchAttribute), over raw HTTP on worker protocol 1.20 in a fresh namespace that registers one datetime attribute. Each datetime value is written on a workflow start and by a first workflow task's upsert_search_attributes command. A value with a UTC offset is stored as the instant it names (workflow#898, fixed in Core 2.15.1); the offset may be written +HH:MM, +HHMM or +HH; a value without one is read as UTC; T may be a space or lowercase; fractional seconds are truncated to microseconds; an RFC 2822 date is accepted; an empty value stores nothing; an unparsable value is refused. A visibility query filters by the stored instant. An upsert reaching exactly 100 attributes, or exactly 65536 value bytes, is accepted; one more is rejected 422 invalid_workflow_stream_command with the limit message and records nothing. Embedded applications have no worker protocol or HTTP registry.",
